# Input
```vue
<!-- should generate diagnostics -->
<template>
  <button @click="$emit('change', value1, value2)">Change</button>
  <button @click="$emit('update', a, b, c)">Update</button>
</template>

<script>
export default {
  emits: ["change", "update"],
};
</script>

```

# Diagnostics
```
invalid-template.vue:3:43 lint/nursery/useVueSingleEventPayload ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

  ! The event change is emitted with more than one value.
  
    1 │ <!-- should generate diagnostics -->
    2 │ <template>
  > 3 │   <button @click="$emit('change', value1, value2)">Change</button>
      │                                           ^^^^^^
    4 │   <button @click="$emit('update', a, b, c)">Update</button>
    5 │ </template>
  
  i A listener written inline in a template, such as @change="onChange($event)", can only read the first value through $event. The other values are lost.
  
  i Put all the values in one object, and send that object instead.
  
  i This rule belongs to the nursery group, which means it is not yet stable and may change in the future. Visit https://biomejs.dev/linter/#nursery for more information.
  

```

